[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Hobbies]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.95]Lesson 46 | 第46课
[00:02.93]Hobbies | 业余爱好
[00:09.56]Who, according to the author, are 'Fortune's favoured children'? | 按照作者的说法，谁是“命运的宠儿”？
[00:16.63]A gifted American psychologist has said, 'Worry is a spasm of the emotion; | 一位有天赋的美国心理学家说过：“忧虑是情绪的一种痉挛；
[00:23.02]the mind catches hold of something and will not let it go.' | 大脑抓住了某样东西就不肯撒手。”
[00:27.45]It is useless to argue with the mind in this condition. | 在这种状态下与大脑争辩是徒劳的。
[00:30.89]The stronger the will, the more futile the task. | 意志越坚强，这种努力就越徒劳。
[00:34.54]One can only gently insinuate something else into its convulsive grasp. | 人们只能巧妙地把别的东西悄悄塞进它痉挛般紧握的手中。
[00:39.98]And if this something else is rightly chosen, if it is really attended by the illumination of another field of interest, | 而如果这别的东西选得恰当，如果它确实伴随着另一兴趣领域的启发之光，
[00:48.31]gradually, and often quite swiftly, the old undue grip relaxes and the process of recuperation and repair begins. | 那么旧有的过度紧握便会逐渐地、而且往往相当迅速地放松，恢复与修复的过程便开始了。
[00:59.30]The cultivation of a hobby and new forms of interest is therefore a policy of the first importance to a public man. | 因此，培养一种业余爱好和新的兴趣形式，对一个从事公务的人来说是头等重要的策略。
[01:07.87]But this is not a business that can be undertaken in a day or swiftly improvised by a mere command of the will. | 但这可不是一天之内就能办成的事，也不是凭意志的一声令下就能仓促促成的。
[01:15.76]The growth of alternative mental interests is a long process. | 另一些精神兴趣的成长是一个漫长的过程。
[01:20.65]The seeds must be carefully chosen; they must fall on good ground; | 种子必须精心挑选；必须播撒在沃土之上；
[01:25.47]they must be sedulously tended, if the vivifying fruits are to be at hand when needed. | 还必须勤加培育，才能在需要时随手摘到那令人焕发生机的果实。
[01:32.62]To be really happy and really safe, one ought to have at least two or three hobbies, and they must all be real. | 要想真正快乐、真正安心，一个人至少应该有两三种爱好，而且都必须是真正的爱好。
[01:40.91]It is no use starting late in life to say: 'I will take an interest in this or that.' | 年纪大了才开始说“我要对这个或那个产生兴趣”是没有用的。
[01:46.63]Such an attempt only aggravates the strain of mental effort. | 这种尝试只会加重精神上的紧张。
[01:51.36]A man may acquire great knowledge of topics unconnected with his daily work, and yet get hardly any benefit or relief. | 一个人可能在与日常工作无关的话题上获得广博的知识，却几乎得不到任何益处或放松。
[02:00.13]It is no use doing what you like; you have got to like what you do. | 做你喜欢的事没有用；你必须喜欢上你所做的事。
[02:04.74]Broadly speaking, human beings may be divided into three classes: | 概括地说，人可以分为三类：
[02:10.27]those who are toiled to death, those who are worried to death, and those who are bored to death. | 累死的、愁死的和烦死的。
[02:18.48]It is no use offering the manual labourer, | 向体力劳动者提供周六下午踢场足球或打场棒球的机会是没有用的，
[02:22.04]tired out with a hard week's sweat and effort the chance of playing a game of football or baseball on Saturday afternoon. | 因为经过一周艰苦的汗水与辛劳，他早已疲惫不堪。
[02:29.96]It is no use inviting the politician or the professional or business man, who has been working or worrying about serious things for six days, | 同样，邀请一位已连续六天为正经事操劳或担忧的政治家、专业人士或商人，
[02:39.87]to work or worry about trifling things at the weekend. | 在周末再去为琐事操劳或担忧，也是没有用的。
[02:44.75]As for the unfortunate people who can command everything they want, | 至于那些能要什么有什么的不幸的人，
[02:49.53]who can gratify every caprice and lay their hands on almost every object of desire--for them a new pleasure a new excitement is only an additional satiation. | 他们能满足每一种突发奇想，几乎能得到每一件渴望之物——对他们来说，一种新的乐趣、一种新的刺激只不过徒增一分餍足罢了。
[03:02.40]In vain they rush frantically round from place to place, trying to escape from avenging boredom by mere clatter and motion. | 他们疯狂地东奔西走，妄图仅凭喧闹与奔波逃避那如影随形、伺机报复的烦闷，结果纯属徒劳。
[03:11.88]For them discipline in one form or another is the most hopeful path. | 对他们来说，某种形式的自律才是最有希望的道路。
[03:18.49]It may also be said that rational, industrious, useful human beings are divided into two classes: | 也可以说，理性的、勤勉的、有用的人分为两类：
[03:26.14]first, those whose work is work and whose pleasure is pleasure; | 第一类人，工作是工作，乐趣是乐趣；
[03:31.20]and secondly, those whose work and pleasure are one. | 第二类人，工作与乐趣合而为一。
[03:35.49]Of these the former are the majority. They have their compensations. | 这两类人前者占多数。他们也有自己的补偿。
[03:40.40]The long hours in the office or the factory bring with them as their reward, | 在办公室或工厂里度过的漫长时光作为回报带来的，
[03:45.46]not only the means of sustenance, but a keen appetite for pleasure even in its simplest and most modest forms. | 不仅是谋生的手段，还有对乐趣的强烈渴求，哪怕是最简单、最朴素的乐趣。
[03:53.80]But Fortune's favoured children belong to the second class. | 但“命运的宠儿”属于第二类。
[03:58.17]Their life is a natural harmony. | 他们的生活是一种天然的和谐。
[04:01.28]For them the working hours are never long enough. | 对他们来说，工作时间永远不够长。
[04:04.92]Each day is a holiday, and ordinary holidays, when they come, are grudged as enforced interruptions in an absorbing vocation. | 天天都是假日，而普通节日的到来反而被抱怨为对一项引人入胜的事业的强制干扰。
[04:15.26]Yet to both classes, the need of an alternative outlook, of a change of atmosphere of a diversion of effort, is essential. | 然而，对这两类人来说，换一种眼光、换一种氛围、换一种努力方向的需要都是必不可少的。
[04:25.22]Indeed, it may well be that those whose work is their pleasure are those who most need the means of banishing it at intervals from their minds. | 的确，那些以工作为乐的人，很可能恰恰是最需要不时把工作从头脑中驱散的人。
